---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`Privacy policy for ${siteConfig.brandName}, including analytics and Google AdSense disclosures.`}
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="meta-row">Last updated {siteConfig.contentUpdated}</p>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <p>
      Calculators run entirely in your browser. We do not upload your project measurements to our servers.
      Shareable result links store values only in the page URL query string on your device.
    </p>
    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      We may store a preference flag (for example, cookie-notice dismissal) in localStorage.
      If the site owner enables Google Analytics 4, GA4 may set cookies to collect usage statistics.
    </p>
    <h2>Google AdSense and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      When AdSense is enabled, Google and third-party vendors use cookies to serve ads based on prior visits to this site or other sites.
      Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visit to this site and/or other sites on the Internet.
      You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting
      <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>
      or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.aboutads.info</a>.
      DoubleClick cookies may be used for ad serving; opt-out information is available via Google’s ads settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      For users in the EEA, UK, and Switzerland, a Google-certified consent management platform (CMP) implementing the IAB TCF is required before personalized ads.
      Configure a CMP before enabling ads for those regions. See the repository file docs/ADSENSE.md for setup steps.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
